d lives of albus  dumbledore you can imagine that it most  certainly did not depict dumbledore in a  favorable manner spilling what she  thought to be a multitude of secrets  about albus and his family  in fact as you may recall this was the  publication which first told readers and  viewers alike about albus dumbledore's  close relationship with the future dark  wizard gelat grindelwald  the life and lives of albus dumbledore  is also the first time we learn about  albus's younger ailing sister  ariana dumbledore  alright so who is ariana dumbledore  aside from being albus's sister we know  that the dumbledore family never sent  her to hogwarts rita skeeter of course  thought that she was a squib a member of  a magical family who does not possess  any magical abilities of their own  this of course was not true ariana  actually had a great deal of power she  just didn't have any control over it as  you may recall from the deathly hallows  ariana was tragically attacked when she  was only six years old by a group of  three young mughals who saw her doing  magic  this attack traumatized ariana to the  point in which she would no longer  perform magic turning her abilities  inward on herself  this was incredibly dangerous and left  her magic uncontrollable as it would  escape from ariana in emotional  outbursts in my harry potter theory  video why harry wasn't an obscurial like  credence i recently discussed how the  description of ariana's illness matches  that of an obscurial so even though she  wasn't referred to as one in the harry  potter series that's most likely because  technically obscurials hadn't been  introduced to the wizarding world canon  yet  but in my opinion she most definitely  could be the inspiration behind credence  and obscurials in any case ariana lived  sequestered away in godric's hollow a  community in which most people didn't  even know that she existed her mother  would only allow her outside during the  dark of night in an effort to keep her  and her unpredictable nature safe it was  here that more tragedy struck the  dumbledore family  one day when ariana and her mother were  the only two home ariana went into a  rage accidentally killing her mother  with an explosion of magic at this point  in her life ariana was only 14 years old  which would be considered quite old for  an obscurial as witches and wizards who  harbour an obscurus typically don't live  into their teenage years that said she  was of course much too young and much  too unstable to live on her own her  father was unable to care for her as he  had been sent to azkaban for assaulting  the young muggles who had attacked  ariana when she was six he never  admitted to the reason behind his crime  before fear that the admission would  result in ariana being locked up so he  sadly died while incarcerated this left  albus as the next in line as her  guardian with great resentment  dumbledore returned to godric tollo to  care for his younger unwell sister  just as his life had been about to get  started  it was not long after while in his care  that ariana lost her life  and so while rita skeeter seemed most  interested in exposing the fact that the  dumbledore family kept ariana hidden  away the real mystery even to those who  were there was in fact who killed ariana  dumbledore for those who may not know  present the time of ariana's death was  albus his younger brother aberforth and  gelet grindelwald you may be thinking  well then it must be quite obvious one  of these three wizards killed ariana  leaving two witnesses to testify and  corroborate each other's stories and yet  it is not quite so simple as that here  in aberforth's words you see how the  events of that terrible day are anything  but clear i pulled out my wand and he  pulled out his and i had the cruciatus  curse used on me by my brother's best  friend  and albus was trying to stop him and  then all three of us were dueling and  the flashing lights and the bangs set  her off she couldn't stand it  the color was draining from aberfor's  face as though he had suffered a mortal  wound  and i think she wanted to help but she  didn't really know what she was doing  and i don't know which of us did it it  could have been any of us and she was  dead so aberforth names himself albus  and grindelwald as the three wizards who  could have killed her and yet he isn't  at all certain in fact none of them are  years later while visiting harry in  death even albus admits that he never  fully knew who killed her in truth he  was always immensely fearful of what had  actually happened that day  it was the truth i feared you see i  never knew which of us in that last  horrific fight had actually cast the  curse that killed my sister i dreaded  beyond all things the knowledge that it  had been i who brought about her death  so it seems that we will never know the  truth of who whether it was one of her  brothers or gelet ended ariana's life  and yet it would be so easy to blame  grindelwald future dark wizard who  harboured ill will towards others whom  he didn't see as his equal we see this  demonstrated again and again throughout  the fantastic beasts series  so why should we assume that he would  have viewed ariana any differently  well my answer to that is if she was in  fact an obscurial he may have valued the  powerful dark magic that existed inside  of her similarly to how he values  credence in fantastic beasts so then  perhaps it would be easiest to say that  it truly was an accident with no one to  blame ariana was tragically in the wrong  place at the wrong time unable to  control her parasitical magic in the  face of such an intense fight the three  wizards would have had to have done  something to protect themselves from her  outburst  after all she had previously killed her  mother in a similar explosion of emotion  so an accident a reflex from one or  possibly all three men in an effort to  shield themselves from harm seems  reasonable  in which case we again can't clearly  name one of them as clearly responsible  for her death seems likely that we'll  never truly know how it all unfolded we  can simply narrow it down to three  possibilities but before i wrap up this  video let me leave you with one more  thought if ariana was an obscurial is it  not possible that her final outburst of  uncontrollable emotion and power is what  killed her think about it when an  obscurial releases its obscurus it's  most often released as an invisible  destructive wind so even though  fantastic beasts credence physically  transforms into his obscurus this type  of transformation is only known to  happen in extremely rare cases meaning  that ariana could have released her  obscurus without anyone seeing it only  to meet her own end after all most  obscurials did not survive their youth  so perhaps neither the dumbledore  brothers nor gaelic grindelwald killed  her at all  perhaps ariana is the one responsible  for her own death  and with that we're at the end of  another video as always i'd love to know  what you think let me know your thoughts  in the comments below and as always if  you enjoyed the video don't forget to  like and subscribe to the channel until  next time remember  happiness can be found even in the  darkest of times if one only remembers  to turn on the light  [Music]  you

